	<body bgcolor="#ffffff" text="#000000">
		<h1 class="largetext">Rodcetnife.org Forums</h1>
		<h2 class="normaltext">General Category => General Discussion => Topic started by: kensai on August 08, 2005, 04:43:13 am</h2>

		<table width="90%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
			<tr>
				<td>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Saying Hello</b><br />
					Post by: <b>kensai</b> on <b>August 08, 2005, 04:43:13 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Hi everyone,<br />For those old timers and those new alike. I just want to say I really miss playing on Rodcet Nife. I am now trying to play EQ 2, I must say some of the quest are abit challenging. Well anyways I still have an account of Rodcet Nife. Take care everyone, /em misses alot of you maybe not enzyme&nbsp; :banghead2: Well later you hard core gamers. I still stick by my earlier post on black listing grasshopa :wtf: Be cool and keep grinding. I will probably be back after I start hating EQ 2.<br /><br />Kensai lvl 60 monk<br />Mastiphal lvl 55 SK</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Saying Hello</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Kinladar</b> on <b>August 09, 2005, 08:54:21 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Rodcet Nife is no more... her server bones scattered to the four corners of the ever shrinking server empire.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Saying Hello</b><br />
					Post by: <b>kocher_aod</b> on <b>August 09, 2005, 05:49:25 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Wow, Kensai,&nbsp; I haven&#039;t seen you in forever.&nbsp; What server you on in eq2?<br /></div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Saying Hello</b><br />
					Post by: <b>kensai</b> on <b>August 10, 2005, 02:17:06 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">hey kocher,<br />I am on oggok, and yes i am lame i kept all the same names of all of my character&#039;s. kensai monk, mastiphal sk, syphon necro and so forth. I think the armor looks very lame, and its a pain to get money. i mean once you get a million pp you dont want to look back. its kind of cool being a noob and no body is really twinked out yet. ive found alot of peeps on the server i am on have not got clue how to assist or lead raids. macro whats a macro, but most folks are nice and want to help each other. its kind of like the blind leading the blind. i am going to stick it out for a little while longer. if not ill be heading back to eq1 again. take care my friend<br /><br />kensai</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Saying Hello</b><br />
					Post by: <b>kocher_aod</b> on <b>August 10, 2005, 04:41:15 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">Damn!&nbsp; I was on Oggok until 2 weeks ago.&nbsp; I move logged over to the Station exchange server.&nbsp; Found a good amount of old RN people here on exchange.&nbsp; Didn&#039;t run into many/any on Oggok.&nbsp; </div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: Saying Hello</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Naithein</b> on <b>August 11, 2005, 12:16:28 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;">[Rodcet Nife is no more... her server bones scattered to the four corners of the ever shrinking server empire]<br /><br />Basically...Our name got screwed and we became one with the Force.<br /><br />I mean Quellious.</div>
					<br /><br />
